    92	## Canonical files and write ownership
    93	
    94	The six top-level Markdown files have disjoint jobs:
    95	
    96	- `README.md` — short project orientation and public-progress pointer.
    97	- `COORDINATION.md` — live process, roles, gates, clocks, and bootstrap.
    98	- `APPROACHES.md` — canonical avenue inventory and comparative ranking:
    99	  routes, gaps, promise, and tried/untried status.
   100	- `AUDIT.md` — promoted-claim and trust-boundary ledger, including
   101	  corrections. Promotion requires the review rule below.
   102	- `PROGRESS.md` — one compact digest per calendar day, newest first.
   103	- `notes.md` — append-oriented tick log and active-state journal.
   104	
   105	The newest `LIVE STATE` block in `notes.md` is authoritative for lanes, holds,
   106	provisional claims, review debt, clocks, and the immediate queue. `xmodel/`
   107	holds immutable producer, reviewer, sweep, and round reports; code and replay
   108	artifacts live beside the relevant cases. `ops/FLEET.md` owns machine inventory
   109	and compute safety rules.
   110	
   111	Do not maintain a second live queue, avenue map, or evidence ledger. Link to
   112	the canonical entry instead of copying it. When a digest must repeat a fact,
   113	label its date and evidence/lifecycle state; later corrections supersede but do
   114	not erase the historical record.
