   148	## Two independent claim axes
   149	
   150	Never conflate mathematical evidence with workflow maturity.
   151	
   152	**Evidence tier** describes what the artifact proves, for example `EXACT`,
   153	`PROVED`, `MOD-p`, `BOOK-RELATIVE`, `FORMAL`, `INTERNAL-UNREVIEWED`, or
   154	`CONJECTURE`. Absence of a certificate means the lower tier. A computational
   155	header or model verdict never upgrades the underlying artifact.
   156	
   157	**Lifecycle state** describes scrutiny:
   158	
   159	`DRAFT -> PRODUCER-CHECKED -> PROVISIONAL -> PROMOTED`
   160	
   161	with exits to `QUARANTINED` or `REFUTED`. `PROVISIONAL` is not an evidence
   162	tier and must never be presented as promoted truth.
   163	
   164	A result may enter `PROVISIONAL` only when all of the following are recorded:
   165	
   166	1. an exact statement and scope, with failed or excluded stronger readings;
   167	   the ambient ring, quotient/localization/saturation order, and every
   168	   specialization must be literal. A conclusion moved between rings must
   169	   exhibit and audit the map; matching variable names are not a map;
   170	2. explicit dependencies and provenance;
   171	3. frozen source/artifact hashes and a replay command when computational;
   172	4. producer-run attacks, sanity checks, and at least one meaningful negative
   173	   control where the object admits one;
   174	5. for a characteristic-`p`, Witt, or `p`-adic successor digit, the exact
   175	   integer numerator, its divisibility on the charged predecessor scheme, and
   176	   the reduced integer quotient are recorded before any reduction modulo `p`;
   177	6. no known contradiction with the current ledgers.
   178	7. **Completion handshake.** An author's hash or “ready” message is advisory
   179	   while that author is still running. The packet is frozen only after the
   180	   author is idle/completed and the coordinator independently verifies its
   181	   seal, replay in every declared mode, and unchanged pre/post hashes. No
   182	   reviewer, commit, or downstream consumer may charge preliminary bytes.
   183	8. **Transactional local publication.** New reports authored by local agents
   184	   or the coordinator use `ops/artifact_finalize.py` by default:
   185	   `begin -> close -> finalize -> verify`. Authors write only the leased
   186	   private partial; the tracked read-only manifest accompanies the final
   187	   report. Root verifies after author completion and runs `verify --staged`
   188	   on the explicitly staged report/manifest before commit. This supplements,
   189	   rather than replaces, replay and hostile mathematical review. Existing
   190	   external `ops/lane.sh` custody remains unchanged until a separate adapter
   191	   migration is reviewed; do not retrofit the transaction into a live lane.
   192	
   193	## Promotion and adversarial review
   194	
   195	1. **Different-model promotion.** No result enters `AUDIT.md` as promoted
   196	   until a different model has performed hostile review. Self-review and two
   197	   agents backed by the same producing model do not satisfy this rule.
   198	2. **Recompute, do not defer.** Review the exact source statement, hypotheses,
   199	   transcription, code, certificate, and conclusion as applicable. A second
   200	   prose opinion is not a computational review.
   201	   For a characteristic-`p`, Witt, or `p`-adic successor residual, independently
   202	   reconstruct the integer quotient and compare its generated rows with the
   203	   exact source identity on both a symbolic control and, where possible, an
   204	   old-pass/new-fail negative control. A mod-`p` bracket calculation alone does
   205	   not review a divided carry.
   206	3. **Priority by exposure.** Review priority is proportional to
   207	   `downstream fanout x centrality x fragility x rollback cost`. A claim that
   208	   many active lanes consume outranks an isolated lemma of equal apparent
   209	   importance.
   210	4. **Latency targets.** Start review as soon as a claim becomes provisional.
   211	   Aim to resolve high-fanout claims within six hours and ordinary claims by
   212	   the next full ideation round. A miss is review debt, recorded in `LIVE
   213	   STATE`; it is not silent permission to promote.
   214	5. **Immutable review inputs.**  Give every background reviewer a frozen,
   215	   hash-pinned claim packet (including the exact canonical excerpts it may
   216	   need) and require it to review those bytes.  Do not make a long review
   217	   depend on rereading mutable live ledgers, and do not freeze canonical
   218	   promotion while that review runs.  Later ledger changes are queued for a
   219	   delta review if they alter the charged claim; unrelated drift is not a
   220	   custody failure.
   221	6. **Fail closed.** `REFUTED` triggers immediate rollback. `GAP` preserves only
   222	   the portion actually checked. Corrections are appended promptly to
   223	   `notes.md`, the relevant canonical route/evidence file, and the current
   224	   daily digest.
   225	
   226	When the current reduction architecture is discussed, use the scoped names
   227	`G2-PSC` (global packet/sheet transport and fidelity) and `G2-BD`
   228	(post-residue-A bounded delay), never bare `G2`. The detailed dependency map
   229	is `ladder/REDUCTION.md`; summaries elsewhere must preserve its arrow
   230	directions and scope.
   231	
   232	## Speculative parallelism and rollback
   233	
   234	Review runs in the background. Once a claim is provisional, cheap and
   235	reversible dependent exploration may begin under a visible speculative
   236	budget:
   237	
   238	- at most three child lanes and one unreviewed dependency generation per
   239	  provisional claim;
   240	- at most six active provisional roots campaign-wide;
   241	- normally no more than 25% of active research capacity may depend on any one
   242	  unreviewed claim;
   243	- enqueue hostile review before launching the first dependent child; a missed
   244	  review deadline freezes new descendants but not unrelated work;
   245	- cap each speculative child at six hours unless the coordinator records a
   246	  reasoned exception;
   247	- publication, promotion, irreversible action, expensive fleet campaigns, and
   248	  further fanout must not rely on an unreviewed claim;
   249	- every dependent report labels the assumption `PROVISIONAL`, so descendants
   250	  can be found and rolled back mechanically.
   251	
   252	The coordinator maintains a lightweight claim DAG in the newest `LIVE STATE`
   253	block: claim ID, exact scope, evidence tier, lifecycle, parents, owner,
   254	reviewer, artifact hashes, descendants, and stop condition. If a premise is
   255	refuted or narrowed, quarantine its descendants immediately, retain them as
   256	conditional work when useful, and re-root any result whose proof did not
   257	actually need the failed premise.
   258	
   259	For each load-bearing bridge, prefer three concurrent attacks when useful and
   260	affordable: prove it, falsify it on the cheapest honest model, and bypass it by

