   263	## The continuous outer loop
   264	
   265	Cadences below are maximum quiet intervals, never reasons to wait. Any event
   266	may interrupt the current allocation; unrelated work continues.
   267	
   268	### Event triggers and micro-rounds
   269	
   270	Run an immediate strategy update when any of these occurs:
   271	
   272	- a decisive lane confirms, refutes, gaps, caps, or times out;
   273	- a new mathematical object, theorem, countermodel, certificate, or materially
   274	  faster instrument is banked;
   275	- review changes a claim's scope or lifecycle;
   276	- an external result or actor changes correctness, route rank, priority,
   277	  publication posture, available artifacts, or competitive status;
   278	- the active portfolio is stalled, duplicated, or exposed to one fragile
   279	  premise beyond the limits above;
   280	- campaign machinery loses or delays state, duplicates work, misroutes a
   281	  model or compute job, exposes mutable inputs, materially inflates context or
   282	  cost, or reports fleet/lane state unreliably.  Treat this as a bounded
   283	  systems micro-round unless it also changes the mathematical ranking.
   284	
   285	A targeted response to a routine local event is a **micro-round**: triage the
   286	delta, launch or stop bounded work, and bank it without forcing every ideator
   287	to rescan all avenues. It does not reset the 12-hour clock. A credible external
   288	proof/counterexample, a load-bearing review reversal, or a new result changing
   289	the global ranking or critical-path hypotheses is critical and starts a full
   290	round immediately, subject to the coalescing rule below. A new promoted entry
   291	alone does not force a whole-portfolio rescan. Other events start a full round when they
   292	materially change the global ranking; otherwise they receive a micro-round.
   293	
   294	Prospective48-hour trial from September6 12:55Z: routine scoped lemmas and
   295	instrument instantiations receive targeted review plus the theorem-interface
   296	composition pass, not an automatic full scan solely because promotion is new.
   297	This changes no hostile-review gate, critical scope-reversal response, or
   298	12-hour completed-round backstop, and does not excuse earlier cadence debt.
   299	Track full scans avoided, integration time and review latency; revert if
   300	important cross-route consequences are missed. The coordinator must record
   301	the ranking/critical-path assessment when choosing a micro-round.
   302	
   303	Coalesce echo events to prevent review/round thrashing. If a sealed full-round
   304	packet already states a provisional result's complete mathematical content and
   305	the post-cutoff review merely confirms that same content and scope, harvest the
   306	lifecycle promotion as a micro-round; it does not trigger an otherwise
   307	identical full scan. A refutation or scope change of a **promoted or
   308	load-bearing** claim, a new dependency on the critical path, or a materially
   309	rank-changing review fact remains a critical trigger. An expected negative
   310	first-gate result or correction to an unpromoted provisional formula may be
   311	coalesced when the global ranking and trust perimeter are unchanged. Record
   312	the coalescing decision explicitly in the next synthesis or `LIVE STATE`.
   313	
   314	Every new provisional or promoted theorem also triggers a **theorem-interface
   315	composition pass**.  Normalize it to object, hypotheses, field/ring, degree or
   316	support bounds, and conclusion; search the claim DAG for results whose
   317	conclusions discharge those hypotheses or whose hypotheses consume the new
   318	conclusion; and test the cheapest exact pairings before treating the theorem
   319	as an isolated endpoint.  Record a new bridge, a scope mismatch, or `NO HIT`.
   320	This pass is bounded and does not interrupt unrelated work.  In particular,
   321	compare proof-side degree/automorphy theorems with counterexample-side
   322	integrality, specialization, compactness, and collision lemmas: their labels
   323	may differ even when their theorem interfaces compose.
   324	
   325	If a critical event arrives during an open full round and invalidates a
   326	load-bearing snapshot assumption, mark that round `ABORTED` and reseal. If it
   327	does not invalidate the packet, take any safe emergency action, finish the
   328	sealed round, and start an immediate follow-on full round. Never mutate the
