   331	### Full-spectrum ideation — at least every 12 hours
   332	
   333	No more than 12 hours may pass between completed full rounds. A significant
   334	event starts one sooner. Each round follows this protocol:
   335	
   336	1. **Freeze a state packet.** Record UTC time, clean basis commit, newer local
   337	   hashes if any, newest `LIVE STATE`, active/recent lane reports, review debt,
   338	   current `APPROACHES.md`, load-bearing `AUDIT.md` corrections, and all new
   339	   external evidence since the prior round.
   340	2. **Blind independent scan.** Every active research agent is a core ideator by
   341	   default and reads the whole avenue map, current gaps, and new evidence
   342	   before seeing the other submissions. A noninterruptible compute or review
   343	   worker may be omitted explicitly; mark the round degraded if this leaves
   344	   inadequate coverage. A rotating specialist lens may be added only after
   345	   the common scan. Model diversity is preferred; duplicate instances still
   346	   think independently.
   347	   After the September6 1210Z round, the automatic whole-portfolio roster is
   348	   Astra, Fable, and Sol. Opus and Grok are bounded utility seats and may be
   349	   invited for a concrete additional lens. Current1210Z invitations remain.
   350	   Whole-portfolio models are invited automatically. Each receives the
   351	   same sealed packet, submission contract, tool boundary, and deadline, and
   352	   must submit before seeing any other lane's report.  Every submission
   353	   receives equal post-deduplication consideration: model identity is neither
   354	   a bonus nor a vote, and operational unavailability degrades but does not
   355	   block the round.
   356	3. **Required submission contract.** Each report gives:
   357	   - a compact disposition vector over every numbered avenue: `unchanged`,
   358	     `raise`, `lower`, or `reopen`, with reasons for every change;
   359	   - a reranking of the principal proof and disproof bottlenecks;
   360	   - one genuinely new mechanism, or an explicit `NO_NEW_MECHANISM` with
   361	     evidence that the best use of capacity is an existing unresolved target;
   362	   - at least one new connection between existing avenues;
   363	   - the strongest proof attack and strongest counterexample/falsification
   364	     attack;
   365	   - one software acceleration or decisive experiment;
   366	   - a short campaign-systems check, independent of the mathematical software
   367	     proposal: either an `UPGRADE` card with the smallest useful test or
   368	     implementation, or `NO_CHANGE` with evidence.  Rotate across state
   369	     freshness, context and retrieval cost, claim/review propagation,
   370	     duplication, model routing and utilization, adapter reliability, AWS
   371	     scheduling and cost, reproducibility, and operator/chat-summary quality;
   372	   - no more than three detailed idea cards, each with explicit dependencies,
   373	     cheapest discriminator, interpretation of each outcome, stop condition,
   374	     and expected information gain;
   375	   - a `continue / redesign / stop` recommendation for current major lanes.
   376	4. **Deduplicate after collection.** Fingerprint ideas by target obstruction,
   377	   mechanism, object, and decisive test. Merge operational duplicates while
   378	   preserving independent origins, disagreements, and genuinely different proof
   379	   mechanisms. Shared wording is not independent support.
   380	5. **Cross-pollinate adversarially.** Only after blind collection, ask lanes to
   381	   combine compatible ideas, expose shared hidden assumptions, attack the
   382	   strongest proposal, and design the cheapest experiment that separates the
   383	   leading choices.
   384	6. **Run the canonical history/priority checksum.** Before compute, search
   385	   `AUDIT.md`, `APPROACHES.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the newest `LIVE STATE`,
   386	   `ladder/REDUCTION.md`, and repository reports for every surviving target,
   387	   mechanism, and close synonym. Reconcile the master known-degree/closed-case
   388	   ledgers, then check each load-bearing literature claim in primary text.
   389	   Label every card `NEW`, `KNOWN`, `DUPLICATE`, or `SCOPE-CONFLICT` in the
   390	   synthesis. Blind consensus never overrides a banked exact result or primary
   391	   theorem; a shared stale packet premise is correlated error, not a vote.
   392	7. **Synthesize and launch.** The coordinator writes a ranked synthesis,
   393	   updates the avenue/claim graphs if needed, assigns owners and reviewers,
   394	   launches reversible lanes immediately, and records why alternatives were
   395	   deferred or stopped.  Deduplicate the systems checks, choose at most one
   396	   highest-value bounded upgrade for immediate work, and track it only in the
