   233	## 4. The field Euler lemma used in both regimes
   234	
   235	If monic P,Q in E[Y] have degrees m,n and obey
   236	
   237	```text
   238	EP=mhP, EQ=nhQ, E=p*d_p+h*Y*d_Y, h!=0,
   239	[P,Q]_(Y,p)=0,
   240	```
   241	
   242	then p[P,Q]=h(nP_Y Q-mP Q_Y). Consequently the Y derivative of
   243	Q^m/P^n is zero, and monicity forces Q^m=P^n. UFD in the FIELD ring
   244	E[Y] gives P=W^(m/d), Q=W^(n/d) for monic W of degree d=gcd(m,n).
   245	No claim that this holds unchanged over a nilpotent ring is made.
   246	
   247	For m6,n10 and
   248	
   249	```text
   250	P=(Y²+b)³+uY+v,
   251	```
   252	
   253	the monic quadratic W has zero linear coefficient, by P's Y5 term;
   254	its constant is b, by the Y4 coefficient3b. Hence u=v=0. The common-
   255	quadratic example alone does not defeat THIS special initial shape.
   256	For m3,n5, a depressed P=Y³+v forces W=Y and v=0.
